    "text": "The survey's images show the same thing. Each pixel shares about a fifth of its noise with the next one, and the bigger the patch you add up, the further the map falls short. A map with one number per pixel can't record how pixels move together. So you measure the factor on the image itself, and widen the error bars by it.",
